WEBVTT

00:02:08.420 --> 00:02:10.630
So we're heading to the chemistry lab next?

00:02:13.920 --> 00:02:15.850
No need to head over there today.

00:02:15.850 --> 00:02:18.910
We'll be going over the answers to the homework in the classroom.

00:02:20.610 --> 00:02:22.250
We had homework?

00:02:22.250 --> 00:02:23.910
Yes, we did.

00:02:24.250 --> 00:02:26.500
Crap, I didn't do it!

00:02:40.250 --> 00:02:42.590
What the hell is she doing?

00:02:43.260 --> 00:02:44.980
Um...

00:02:44.980 --> 00:02:46.480
Is somethin' the matter?

00:02:49.450 --> 00:02:51.020
She's a cryin' mess!

00:02:53.460 --> 00:02:56.570
Um... I think it was...

00:02:56.570 --> 00:02:57.550
Oba-san?

00:02:58.230 --> 00:02:59.810
You know her name?

00:02:59.810 --> 00:03:02.050
You're Oba Minato-san, aren't you?

00:03:04.870 --> 00:03:06.670
Oh?

00:03:06.670 --> 00:03:09.410
You didn't remember, Torako-san?

00:03:09.410 --> 00:03:10.430
Not at all.

00:03:13.320 --> 00:03:15.920
Oba-san, what's the matter?

00:03:18.620 --> 00:03:24.600
Um, you see, I dropped a hundred yen coin...

00:03:24.600 --> 00:03:29.470
And now... I can't reach it...

00:03:31.100 --> 00:03:33.480
You're kidding me!  That's it?!

00:03:34.920 --> 00:03:38.190
Are you an idiot?  That's not something to cry about.

00:03:42.960 --> 00:03:44.470
I'm sorry!  I got it!

00:03:44.470 --> 00:03:47.570
It sure is sad to lose 100 yen!

00:03:47.570 --> 00:03:52.060
Here, I can at least spare 100 yen, so...

00:03:56.090 --> 00:03:57.720
What do you want to drink?

00:04:04.610 --> 00:04:06.300
Cocoa.

00:04:08.010 --> 00:04:08.950
Here.

00:04:14.480 --> 00:04:16.270
Thank you!

00:04:40.350 --> 00:04:41.800
Torako!

00:04:44.050 --> 00:04:45.560
Good morning!

00:04:48.050 --> 00:04:49.180
Hey!

00:04:49.420 --> 00:04:51.640
Here's your 100 yen back.

00:04:59.620 --> 00:05:01.020
What?

00:05:01.020 --> 00:05:02.880
Your bag's not too heavy?

00:05:02.880 --> 00:05:04.820
I could carry it for you.

00:05:05.990 --> 00:05:08.530
No, I'm good.

00:05:08.900 --> 00:05:10.130
I see...

00:05:12.920 --> 00:05:14.160
Torako!

00:05:15.500 --> 00:05:18.460
Let me carry that for you.

00:05:20.200 --> 00:05:21.800
Here, have a towel.

00:05:23.660 --> 00:05:24.590
Here.

00:05:24.590 --> 00:05:26.380
Go ahead.

00:05:28.740 --> 00:05:30.050
Use this.

00:05:30.340 --> 00:05:31.720
You can have this!

00:05:32.740 --> 00:05:34.680
What's with her?

00:05:37.390 --> 00:05:39.830
What has been up with them all morning?

00:05:40.490 --> 00:05:42.020
Don't ask me.

00:05:43.920 --> 00:05:45.500
Hey, Torako.

00:05:46.220 --> 00:05:48.700
About that CD I lent you...

00:05:58.530 --> 00:05:59.960
Ushio!

00:06:02.960 --> 00:06:04.920
Wait, Ushio!

00:06:12.320 --> 00:06:13.810
Oh, I see.

00:06:15.460 --> 00:06:18.510
You lent her something too.

00:06:19.060 --> 00:06:20.280
Yeah...

00:06:20.730 --> 00:06:22.900
Who could have known?

00:06:22.900 --> 00:06:25.240
What'd you lend her?

00:06:25.240 --> 00:06:28.790
Me?  Me...

00:06:34.460 --> 00:06:36.980
She didn't know how to buy a train ticket.

00:06:36.980 --> 00:06:40.880
So I helped her out when she was sobbing in front of the ticket gates.

00:06:43.100 --> 00:06:46.340
Ever since then she's been going full steam trying to pay me back.

00:06:46.340 --> 00:06:48.520
Something is wrong with her.

00:06:49.940 --> 00:06:51.470
I found you!

00:06:52.140 --> 00:06:53.670
Let's go home together!

00:06:53.670 --> 00:06:55.160
She's here!

00:06:56.310 --> 00:06:57.390
Oda Minato

00:06:57.390 --> 00:06:59.310
Staying away from Oda Minato

00:07:00.330 --> 00:07:02.480
The first plan is this.

00:07:02.820 --> 00:07:07.230
Convince her that "I'm actually a horrible person."

00:07:07.230 --> 00:07:10.560
Try and aim to use up all her gratitude.

00:07:10.560 --> 00:07:12.070
Like how, exactly?

00:07:12.070 --> 00:07:13.740
Minato...

00:07:15.690 --> 00:07:18.560
I don't got no money, see...

00:07:18.560 --> 00:07:21.060
Can you spare a dime for some juice?

00:07:21.060 --> 00:07:23.830
Sorry, I don't have any money either.

00:07:24.530 --> 00:07:25.940
Oh, really?

00:07:26.490 --> 00:07:28.420
Then what good are ya!

00:07:29.660 --> 00:07:31.270
S-Sorry!

00:07:31.270 --> 00:07:33.260
I'll bring some money tomorrow, promise!

00:07:33.260 --> 00:07:35.870
So, please...

00:07:37.750 --> 00:07:41.500
Just kidding!  I wasn't serious!  It was a joke!

00:07:41.530 --> 00:07:44.470
What kind of a farce is that?

00:07:44.470 --> 00:07:46.750
It's impossible for Torako-san.

00:07:47.230 --> 00:07:51.070
Staying away from Oda Minato

00:07:50.390 --> 00:07:52.500
Not yet up to 2, I see.

00:07:52.500 --> 00:07:54.410
It's fractional!

00:07:54.620 --> 00:07:56.150
It is not impossible!

00:07:56.150 --> 00:07:58.240
So what if I failed once or twice?

00:07:58.240 --> 00:08:01.700
This time I'll become a "Terrible Bastard" for real!

00:08:01.700 --> 00:08:02.840
Oh yeah?

00:08:05.330 --> 00:08:07.550
Hey, girlie...

00:08:11.030 --> 00:08:16.500
High school girls sure are nicely developed these days, eh?

00:08:20.430 --> 00:08:22.160
Hey, bend over a sec.

00:08:24.220 --> 00:08:27.690
Your old man's is in need of some cash now, I hear.

00:08:27.690 --> 00:08:31.200
Think you'd be interested in handling a little shady job for me instead?

00:08:31.200 --> 00:08:32.860
Off-the-record...

00:08:33.210 --> 00:08:35.390
A shady job?

00:08:44.330 --> 00:08:46.760
What the heck!  What's so funny?!

00:08:47.390 --> 00:08:48.710
Are ya makin' fun of me?

00:08:53.560 --> 00:08:54.740
She wants to do it?

00:09:05.190 --> 00:09:07.290
I win!

00:09:07.290 --> 00:09:08.690
Win?  Win what?

00:09:09.140 --> 00:09:10.530
A staring contest.

00:09:10.530 --> 00:09:13.740
That is not a game that high school students play.

00:09:13.740 --> 00:09:15.510
Now look here...

00:09:14.020 --> 00:09:17.950
It seems like they're on the same wavelength.

00:09:22.950 --> 00:09:25.480
Well, it's not like I failed.

00:09:25.480 --> 00:09:30.790
That was just for the purpose of collecting data on the enemy!

00:09:30.790 --> 00:09:32.630
You got a problem with that?

00:09:32.630 --> 00:09:36.130
And what might that data have led you to conclude?

00:09:36.400 --> 00:09:37.550
This!

00:09:37.550 --> 00:09:41.910
"With my cool demeanor, I simply do not care" plan!

00:09:42.660 --> 00:09:45.180
What kind of plan is this exactly?

00:09:45.480 --> 00:09:46.970
Well, you see...

00:09:50.980 --> 00:09:53.330
Torako, what's next?

00:09:53.820 --> 00:09:55.080
What?

00:09:55.080 --> 00:09:56.740
Tatsuki-chan, say something.

00:09:57.440 --> 00:10:00.050
Say something?  Like what?

00:10:00.050 --> 00:10:03.580
You know, that cool attitude you're so good at.

00:10:05.790 --> 00:10:07.960
Do not "Oh!" me!

00:10:10.210 --> 00:10:11.970
I'm beggin' ya!

00:10:15.510 --> 00:10:17.390
Oba-san.

00:10:19.090 --> 00:10:20.960
I have something to say to you.

00:10:20.960 --> 00:10:22.140
What?

00:10:25.090 --> 00:10:27.160
I can't say it!

00:10:27.160 --> 00:10:28.560
Say it like you mean it!

00:10:28.560 --> 00:10:32.380
I do not understand why it is that I must be the one to tell her.

00:10:32.380 --> 00:10:34.410
What, you chicken?

00:10:34.410 --> 00:10:37.030
I am not chicken.  That is not the issue.

00:10:37.280 --> 00:10:38.720
Oh, I see then.

00:10:38.720 --> 00:10:43.440
It's not like you to turn down a request, Ta-chan.

00:10:43.440 --> 00:10:44.930
What a shame, really.

00:10:44.930 --> 00:10:47.870
Your mother doesn't remember raising a child like that....

00:10:46.880 --> 00:10:50.170
And I do not recall having a mother like you!

00:10:51.040 --> 00:10:53.040
Don't bully Torako!

00:10:55.070 --> 00:10:58.510
I don't really understand, but I'll apologize!

00:10:58.810 --> 00:11:00.930
Stop it!

00:10:59.780 --> 00:11:00.930
This is...

00:11:01.250 --> 00:11:03.490
...not bullying...

00:11:03.490 --> 00:11:06.300
...it's being bullied...

00:11:10.390 --> 00:11:12.160
You made up!

00:11:15.310 --> 00:11:17.490
Guess Tatsuki-san is no good either.

00:11:17.490 --> 00:11:19.990
What the heck are they doing?

00:11:27.830 --> 00:11:29.410
Time to try breaking up.

00:11:29.740 --> 00:11:33.080
Stop hangin' around me!

00:11:41.490 --> 00:11:44.380
I ended up giving her a juice to console her.

00:11:44.380 --> 00:11:46.060
She was really crying.

00:11:46.060 --> 00:11:47.610
Are you an idiot?

00:11:51.150 --> 00:11:54.330
If mental plans don't work, then how about a physical one?

00:11:54.330 --> 00:11:55.270
In other words, RUN AWAY!

00:11:58.810 --> 00:12:00.150
Anyway, just run!

00:12:00.150 --> 00:12:01.920
Us too?

00:12:01.920 --> 00:12:03.990
Indeed, why are we running as well?

00:12:04.770 --> 00:12:06.820
Where are you going?

00:12:12.830 --> 00:12:15.040
She's damn fast.

00:12:15.370 --> 00:12:17.540
Wait up, I said!

00:12:18.500 --> 00:12:20.750
At this rate, the "rachi"...

00:12:20.750 --> 00:12:22.140
Wait, what does "rachi" even mean?

00:12:22.140 --> 00:12:24.330
It's the fence surrounding a horse race track.

00:12:24.330 --> 00:12:27.050
So unless you go through an opening or poke through somewhere...

00:12:28.840 --> 00:12:29.960
Thanks info!

00:12:29.960 --> 00:12:31.700
This isn't the time for vocabulary class!

00:12:31.700 --> 00:12:33.450
There's no opening in this "rachi!"

00:12:31.700 --> 00:12:34.890
Note:  Also Japanese expression meaning "we're not getting anywhere."

00:12:33.450 --> 00:12:34.890
That's the expression.

00:12:36.700 --> 00:12:38.520
Who was that just now?

00:12:38.520 --> 00:12:40.810
Some people from the high school, wasn't it?

00:12:40.810 --> 00:12:42.590
Maybe they're playing tag.

00:12:43.480 --> 00:12:46.590
What could they be running from at this point?

00:12:46.590 --> 00:12:49.850
It's not like you can run away from life itself.

00:12:49.850 --> 00:12:52.020
They're just playing tag.

00:12:52.020 --> 00:12:56.200
Now now, if you don't play games seriously, they get boring.

00:12:56.200 --> 00:12:59.590
Think about it.  The thing chasing after you is a real demon.

00:12:59.800 --> 00:13:03.000
And if it catches you, it'll steal away your shirikodama.

00:12:59.950 --> 00:13:07.800
Note: The shirikodama is a fictional life force located inside one's rear end that kappa (Japanese lake monster) would steal to make you drown.

00:13:04.440 --> 00:13:06.360
I thought kappa stole those?

00:13:07.800 --> 00:13:10.460
Under Construction

00:13:07.800 --> 00:13:10.460
Entry Prohibited

00:13:14.270 --> 00:13:16.830
The difference between us and her...

00:13:16.830 --> 00:13:19.270
...is her height!

00:13:19.270 --> 00:13:20.820
Good thinking.

00:13:21.480 --> 00:13:24.610
And yet, we have nothing to do with this.

00:13:24.910 --> 00:13:27.220
Running like this is hard...

00:13:30.780 --> 00:13:32.990
She's smiling for some reason!

00:13:34.870 --> 00:13:36.790
Torako!

00:13:37.920 --> 00:13:39.630
Wait!

00:13:45.280 --> 00:13:46.530
I caught you!

00:13:50.680 --> 00:13:52.670
So, where are we going?

00:13:57.190 --> 00:13:59.940
I can't think of anything else.

00:14:03.290 --> 00:14:04.690
Torako!

00:14:05.710 --> 00:14:07.770
Can I sit next to you?

00:14:07.770 --> 00:14:09.410
Please yourself.

00:14:17.600 --> 00:14:18.910
Suzu?

00:14:26.690 --> 00:14:28.530
What is this?

00:14:28.530 --> 00:14:30.330
What's going on?

00:14:31.140 --> 00:14:37.220
Maybe Suzume-san senses Torako being taken away from her, and doesn't like it.

00:14:38.060 --> 00:14:40.460
A dog whose master has been taken away?

00:14:40.460 --> 00:14:42.900
Quite the popular one, are you not, Torako-san?

00:14:43.200 --> 00:14:47.200
So it's not your problem now?

00:14:47.200 --> 00:14:49.240
It's already someone else's problem...

00:14:50.030 --> 00:14:52.050
What's with this?

00:15:01.230 --> 00:15:03.090
Torako, going to the bathroom?

00:15:03.090 --> 00:15:04.480
I'm gonna come, too!

00:15:07.120 --> 00:15:09.380
I can go all by myself, goddammit!

00:15:09.380 --> 00:15:11.930
So don't follow me!  Damn, you're annoying!

00:15:12.230 --> 00:15:14.830
I think Torako-san's had about enough.

00:15:14.830 --> 00:15:16.770
Everyone has their breaking point.

00:15:16.770 --> 00:15:19.340
And it has already been a number of days.

00:15:19.340 --> 00:15:24.560
Maybe she just gives off those types of pheromones, you know?

00:15:25.680 --> 00:15:28.690
Ushio, let's go to the bathroom together.

00:15:28.690 --> 00:15:29.990
So they come to me?

00:15:30.290 --> 00:15:31.690
Ushio!

00:15:31.690 --> 00:15:33.610
You go together on your own!

00:15:37.520 --> 00:15:40.470
Fine, I guess we'll go by ourselves...

00:15:57.480 --> 00:15:59.330
Hey, Suzume.

00:16:07.670 --> 00:16:10.300
You're not with Torako?

00:16:11.330 --> 00:16:14.290
Suzume, you want some candy?

00:16:14.290 --> 00:16:14.950
Candy...

00:16:50.280 --> 00:16:52.470
Suzume, I'll give you these.

00:16:55.480 --> 00:16:58.960
These are some cookies that the underclassmen made for the student council.

00:16:58.290 --> 00:16:58.950
Cookie!

00:16:58.960 --> 00:17:00.270
Please eat them.

00:17:14.870 --> 00:17:17.480
Hey, I don't need this bread.

00:17:17.480 --> 00:17:19.800
I bought too much and can't eat it all.

00:17:19.810 --> 00:17:20.590
Bread!

00:17:31.680 --> 00:17:32.930
Yuck.

00:17:33.510 --> 00:17:36.610
Saotome-kun, have some juice.

00:17:36.610 --> 00:17:40.370
This is the first time I tried this one, and it's totally not my taste.

00:17:41.050 --> 00:17:41.670
Juice!

00:17:41.850 --> 00:17:44.180
Sorry that I already drank some of it.

00:17:45.220 --> 00:17:48.730
Wait, don't misunderstand!  I'm not trying to get a second-hand kiss or anything!

00:17:48.730 --> 00:17:50.960
I just don't like the flavor, that's all!

00:17:53.290 --> 00:17:55.990
What am I so worried about?

00:17:56.440 --> 00:17:57.880
Wait, but that's...

00:18:04.060 --> 00:18:05.680
Hungry?

00:18:08.220 --> 00:18:10.350
I have some onigiri.  Do you want any?

00:18:10.740 --> 00:18:11.490
Onigiri!

00:18:19.030 --> 00:18:22.440
You should get some exercise, man.

00:18:22.440 --> 00:18:26.300
Don't underestimate the amount of exercise you get in a liberal arts club.

00:18:26.300 --> 00:18:28.830
Exercise doing what exactly?

00:18:29.130 --> 00:18:32.020
When you take a picture, it's "shooting" right?

00:18:32.020 --> 00:18:35.810
Shoot, fire, let fly, hunting, the wild!

00:18:35.810 --> 00:18:38.550
Doesn't it sound really active?

00:18:39.680 --> 00:18:44.080
Isn't that just a word association game?

00:18:45.130 --> 00:18:46.750
Oh, Torako-chan...

00:18:46.750 --> 00:18:47.950
What?

00:18:47.950 --> 00:18:49.400
...'s friend.

00:18:50.630 --> 00:18:51.940
Want some gum?

00:18:52.250 --> 00:18:53.070
Gum!

00:18:53.340 --> 00:18:54.350
Sure.

00:19:00.750 --> 00:19:03.170
Your expression is too stiff.

00:19:03.960 --> 00:19:05.200
Oh, there!

00:19:08.060 --> 00:19:11.450
Hey, Suzunyan.  We meet again.

00:19:13.940 --> 00:19:16.460
Here, have some potato chips.

00:19:16.600 --> 00:19:17.560
Potato Chips!

00:19:24.820 --> 00:19:28.160
What are you doing, Saotome-san?

00:19:28.160 --> 00:19:30.350
Have these Pockily.

00:19:30.530 --> 00:19:31.350
Pockily!

00:19:38.760 --> 00:19:42.240
Suzume-san, what is all that?

00:19:43.720 --> 00:19:46.100
I do not have anything.

00:19:47.730 --> 00:19:49.340
Wait!

00:19:49.340 --> 00:19:51.710
Now that I think about it, Toshiko-san...

00:19:51.980 --> 00:19:52.680
Shortbread!

00:19:52.400 --> 00:19:53.950
Will this do?

00:20:07.810 --> 00:20:10.470
Oh, two came out.

00:20:16.090 --> 00:20:17.020
Here.

00:20:17.240 --> 00:20:17.850
Cocoa!

00:20:24.330 --> 00:20:25.720
What?

00:20:27.150 --> 00:20:29.380
What are you going to do with those?

00:20:30.410 --> 00:20:31.920
I won't give them to you.

00:20:32.440 --> 00:20:33.890
I don't want them!

00:20:39.850 --> 00:20:42.420
Whoa, look at Saotome!

00:20:42.420 --> 00:20:44.670
I'll contribute too.

00:20:44.670 --> 00:20:46.470
Didn't you eat lunch?

00:20:46.670 --> 00:20:49.300
Snacks?  I'll give you some.

00:20:49.360 --> 00:20:50.180
Snack #1

00:20:50.180 --> 00:20:51.060
Snack #2

00:20:51.060 --> 00:20:51.930
Snack #3

00:20:51.930 --> 00:20:52.970
Snack #4

00:21:11.610 --> 00:21:12.920
Here.

00:21:13.790 --> 00:21:16.370
If you'd like, have this as well.

00:21:17.250 --> 00:21:19.360
They're confeitos.

00:21:19.360 --> 00:21:21.020
Home made.

00:21:21.870 --> 00:21:23.970
They're <i>good</i>.

00:21:25.230 --> 00:21:26.910
Confeitos...

00:21:36.460 --> 00:21:40.330
What's this?  Does she plan to eat all of that?

00:21:40.330 --> 00:21:44.450
I've thought that you're one of those big eaters for a while...

00:21:44.450 --> 00:21:48.830
Well, sleeping and eating well raises a good kid, they say...

00:21:49.230 --> 00:21:53.430
It's not like it's my job as your homeroom teacher to make sure you grow up fast...

00:21:53.430 --> 00:21:55.010
Candy?

00:21:55.010 --> 00:21:57.040
Do you want candy?

00:21:57.040 --> 00:21:58.190
Candy, huh?

00:21:59.160 --> 00:22:02.380
I do have some Japanese sweets someone gave me.

00:22:02.720 --> 00:22:03.420
Buns!

00:22:10.860 --> 00:22:13.130
What are you doing, seriously?

00:22:13.750 --> 00:22:15.680
Torako, want a candy?

00:22:15.680 --> 00:22:16.460
Candy.

00:22:17.740 --> 00:22:19.170
Ayumi, want some too?

00:22:20.390 --> 00:22:22.230
I can't, I'll gain weight!

00:23:55.590 --> 00:23:57.230
What's on Hyakko<i> next week?</i>

00:23:57.230 --> 00:23:58.200
"A Winged Tiger!"

00:23:58.500 --> 00:24:00.410
It means something like "A Demon with an Iron Rod?"

00:24:00.410 --> 00:24:01.370
Doesn't it?

00:24:01.370 --> 00:24:03.400
It's finally time to tell Touma-oneechan's story.

00:24:03.400 --> 00:24:04.830
Sorry for waiting so long!

00:24:04.830 --> 00:24:05.960
Yagi-chan, you were waiting?

00:24:05.960 --> 00:24:07.680
Tune in again next time!
